    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0494" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6081: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-15T18:00:00+02:00">October 15, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 15—4:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>246. I attended a luncheon at the British Embassy today given in honor of Anthony
                        Eden<anchor n="15" xml:id="d354-f1"/> who told me he left London Saturday
                    and arrived yesterday. I gathered that the main reason Eden’s visit was to
                    conduct a personal inspection of the defenses of Egypt and the Sudan, but it
                    seems likely that he may also take the occasion to seek to effect an improvement
                    in Anglo-Egyptian relations particularly as regards the attitude of the King by
                    whom Eden said he was being received.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador told me that no reference to Eden’s visit was being permitted in
                    the press.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d354-f1" n="15" xml:id="d354-f1-content">
                <p>British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
